 "JM:10": {
  "id": "ac3a7071-cfa7-459a-a874-123a5b8f992d",
  "text": "If \\(15\\sin^{4}\\alpha+ 10\\cos^{4}\\alpha= 6\\), for some \\(\\alpha\\in R\\), then the value of \\(27\\sec^{6}\\alpha+ 8\\csc^{6}\\alpha\\) is equal to :",
  "context": null,
  "solution": "\\(15\\sin^{4}\\alpha + 10\\cos^{4}\\alpha = 6\\) \\[15\\sin^{4}\\alpha + 10\\cos^{4}\\alpha = 6\\left( \\sin^{2}\\alpha + \\cos^{2}\\alpha \\right)^{2}\\] \\[\\left( 3\\sin^{2}\\alpha - 2\\cos^{2}\\alpha \\right)^{2} = 0\\] \\[\\tan^{2}\\alpha = \\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\cot^{2}\\alpha = \\frac{3}{2}\\] \\[\\Rightarrow 27\\sec^{6}\\alpha + 8{\\csc}^{6}\\alpha\\] \\[= 27\\left( \\sec^{6}\\alpha \\right)^{3} + 8\\left( {\\csc}^{6}\\alpha \\right)^{3}\\] \\[= 27\\left( 1 + \\tan^{2}\\alpha \\right)3 + 8\\left( 1 + \\cot^{2}\\alpha \\right)^{3}\\] \\[= 250\\]",
